            <ArticleTitle>Asymmetric Total Synthesis of (+)-Intricenyne via an Endocyclization Route to Oxocane Skeleton.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6642-6645</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b03370</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The first total synthesis of (+)-intricenyne consisting of an oxocane skeleton was achieved via an extremely selective endocyclization strategy. The key features of the synthesis include a regio- and diastereoselective epoxide opening reaction, concise elaboration of oxocane cores via abnormally selective endocyclization ether ring formation, and versatile incorporation of the labile functional groups.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
